<title>ITALY: Italy's insurer SAI premium income rises.</title>
<headline>Italy's insurer SAI premium income rises.</headline>
<dateline>TURIN, Italy 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian insurance group SAI saw a 7.6 percent rise in premium income to 1.504 trillion lire in the first five months of 1997, chairman Carmelo Caruso told the annual shareholders' meeting.</p>
<p>Italy's largest motor insurance company saw auto premium income rise over seven percent in the period, he added.</p>
<p>Group net profit in 1996 was 94.1 billion lire against 92.1 billion in 1995, on premium income that rose 20 percent to 4.607 trillion lire.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
</text>
